From 4423cb7123e9209237da70c03fbfd537a8ec09ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kepler-llama <kepler-llama@localhost>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 22:31:37 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] cuda: Kepler (sm_30) matrix-vector and attention kernels,
 prompt path and dispatch

mmvk.cu: matrix-vector kernels for 1-8 token columns (Q3_K, Q4_K, Q5_K, Q6_K, Q8_0, Q5_0, IQ3_XXS, F16) and the
attention matvecs (KQ, KQV), tuned for GTX 650 Ti class GPUs (CUDA 10.2, no dp4a, no fast FP16). Selection
variables GGML_CUDA_KEPLER_* (auto by default; off restores the stock path). Prompt processing on cc < 5.0:
row-chunked dequantization and token columns padded to 96 so cuBLAS picks its fast sm_30 kernel
(GGML_CUDA_KEPLER_PP). F32 output for F16 compute without fast FP16; strided/pointer-array batched SGEMM below
cc 5.0. Small dispatch adjustments in common.cuh, fattn-mma-f16.cuh, mmf.cuh, rope.cu, unary.cu.
